our 80s movie is about to have a massive  gaming moment plus a classic from the  n64 is finally coming to the switch all  this and more on today's gamespot news  the terminator will be back in an open  world survival game developed by nikon  milan a young studio with only the title  rims racing under its belt this untitled  terminator game will be set before the  events of judgement day when the war  between humans and machines began the  teaser image shows the t800 the robot  skeleton under arnold schwarzenegger's  synthetic skin in the films but no  detail so far on whether the iconic  actor or any characters from the films  will make an appearance the terminator  isn't the only 80s action movie being  revived by naycom robocop rogue city is  a first-person shooter featuring the  titular cybernetic police officer  faithfully recreating the precision and  brutality scene in the original film it  will be releasing in june 2023 and is  coming to pc ps5 xbox series consoles  and nintendo switch do you love your  quests too but hate the fact that you  have to have a facebook account  connected to it that your weird aunt  keeps sending friend requests to well  starting in august quest users will no  longer need to use their facebook  accounts to log in instead users will  need to create a new meta account in  order to use the headset this move is  all a part of meta's plan to continue  shifting away from the facebook brand as  well as a response to user  dissatisfaction with the facebook  account requirement in addition to login  credentials changing the oculus profile  will evolve into a new customizable  feature called meta horizon profiles  friends will also become followers in a  move made to become similar to  instagram's existing model if you  previously merged your oculus and  facebook account there will be an option  to decouple the two during the new meta  account setup process previously  purchased apps will also immediately be  available so now you can stop the  awkward excuses for not accepting family  members on facebook at thanksgiving and  simply say i don't have an account  anymore while you wait to decouple your  quest headset from your facebook account  why not relax with a little dose of  pokemon nostalgia nintendo has announced  that the n64 game pokemon puzzle league  is coming to nintendo switch online plus  expansion pack on july 15th that's one  week from the time of this recording so  make sure to mark your calendars and  while you've got your calendar open mark  the start of gamescom on august 24  because microsoft has announced it will  be there the company has yet to share  specifics around its plans but it did  confirm xbox will have a place on the  show floor and it will have some news to  share as well about games that have  already been announced according to  gamescom's organizers more than 250  companies are signed on to appear at the  event this year including ubisoft coke  media and bandai namco in terms of  companies that will not attend gamescom  these include nintendo activision  blizzard and sony among others gamescom  2022 will be a hybrid style event that  has both an in-person element and an  online show the opening night live  stream by games media veteran jeff keely  will mark the beginning of the event as  well speaking of jeff keely last year's  game awards ended with the reveal of the  matrix awakening a free unreal 5 demo  for ps5 and xbox series consoles that  demo which allows you to run and drive  around a stunningly realized city will  no longer be available to claim via the  digital storefronts after today friday  july 8th if you've already added the  demo to your library and are worried  about deleting it off of your hard drive  feel free to do so as users that have  redeemed it from digital storefronts can  re-download at their leisure and that is  it for today's gamespot news thank you  everyone so much for joining make sure  to go to gamespot.com to get more  details on all these stories plus a  bunch of other stories that we couldn't  include in today's episode and we'll see  you next week
 

